<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
      292 — account.casdoor_sub: the A5 part-B cross-carrier route-pin fix.

      GAP: the gateway's GatewayRouteAccessFilter builds a per-user identity set
      (userIds) to match casdoor_user route pins (targeted allow/deny rows). For a
      REAL Casdoor-JWT carrier that set includes the raw UUID `sub` claim
      (Roles.casdoorIdOf). For a native-login bff_ session carrier the set is built
      from admin-bff's /bff/internal/session/introspect response, which only carries
      the durable account id — "casdoor:<handle>" with the handle drawn from the
      id_token as email > preferred_username > sub (InternalAccountController
      .SUBJECT_CLAIMS). When the subject came from `email` or `preferred_username`,
      the Casdoor UUID is NOT derivable from the account id AT ALL, so a route pin
      written in UUID form matches the JWT carrier but silently never matches the
      SAME HUMAN arriving via a bff_ session: a UUID-form ALLOW pin wrongly denies
      them, and — worse — a UUID-form DENY pin (a targeted ban) FAILS OPEN for the
      native-login carrier (the A5 part-B asymmetry from the native-login authz
      audit).

      FIX (enrichment, this changeset + the InternalAccountController stamp/read):
      persist the raw Casdoor `sub` on the account row, captured at the ONE place
      the raw id_token is decoded (InternalAccountController#ensureAccount's
      provider="casdoor" branch — the native-login mint path; the session mint at
      POST /sessions only ever receives the accountId, so the account row is the
      only in-repo place the UUID can be captured). Introspect then surfaces it as
      a nullable `casdoorSub` field for the gateway to fold into userIds.

      DELIBERATELY NULLABLE, NO DEFAULT, NO backfill: the UUID is not derivable
      from any existing column (that is the bug), so legacy rows CANNOT be
      backfilled here — they self-heal on the account's next native login, because
      ensureAccount re-runs (and re-stamps) on EVERY sign-in, exactly like the
      roles re-sync. Until then introspect returns casdoorSub=null and the gateway
      degrades to exactly today's behavior. Like changeset 290, auth-core's
      AccountStore INSERT path knows nothing of this column (its AccountRow entity
      has no such field), so NOT NULL would fail every account creation.

      DELIBERATELY NOT UNIQUE (unlike 290/291): the localpart columns gate a
      shared-password homeserver identity, where a collision IS an account
      takeover. casdoor_sub is only ever ADDED to the gateway's pin-match identity
      set under deny-wins semantics (an extra id can only make a matching pin
      APPLY, never remove a deny), and one human's Casdoor UUID can legitimately
      back more than one account row over time (the account id is keyed on the
      email/preferred_username-derived subject, which Casdoor lets the user
      change; the UUID does not change with it). A UNIQUE constraint would turn
      that legitimate re-keying into a login-breaking 500 for zero security gain.

      Portable DDL mirrors the 180-band idiom: addColumn with a
      <rollback><dropColumn>. varchar(64): Casdoor subs are 36-char UUIDs; small
      headroom, no clob. Band 292: next free above 291. Appended LAST.
    -->

    <changeSet id="292-account-casdoor-sub-add-column" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>account.casdoor_sub — the raw Casdoor `sub` UUID captured from the
                 native-login id_token at InternalAccountController#ensureAccount
                 (provider="casdoor"). Nullable (legacy rows self-heal on next
                 native login), NOT unique (see rationale above). Read back by
                 /bff/internal/session/introspect as the nullable casdoorSub field
                 so the gateway can match UUID-form casdoor_user route pins for
                 bff_ session carriers.</comment>
        <addColumn tableName="account">
            <column name="casdoor_sub" type="varchar(64)"/>
        </addColumn>
        <rollback>
            <dropColumn tableName="account" columnName="casdoor_sub"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
